.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt GROUP 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm group
.Nd the group database
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The file
.Pa /etc/group ,
readable by everyone, holds one line per group with four fields
separated by colons:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
name:password:gid:member,member,...
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width password
.It Ar name
The group name.
.It Ar password
A
.Xr crypt 3
hash, almost always
.Ql * :
group passwords are a relic.
.It Ar gid
The group ID.
.It Ar member
The users with this as a supplementary group, separated by commas.
A user's primary group, the
.Ar gid
of its
.Xr passwd 5
entry, is usually not listed.
.El
.Pp
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are ignored, but the tools that rewrite the file do not keep them.
Change the file with
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr groupmod 8
and
.Xr groupdel 8 ,
which take the account database's lock and check the result.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/group -compact
.It Pa /etc/group
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr groups 1 ,
.Xr id 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr pw 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
file format appeared in
.At v6 .
